Fri Oct 23 07:13:08 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.12.0 (upstream tag v0.12.0, 2026-10-23; includes
  v0.10.0, 2026-10-21 and v0.11.0, 2026-10-22):
  * Harden parsers against hostile input (no CVE assigned): bounded
    Matroska chapter/tag recursion, saturating crop/field math on
    Matroska/MXF/AAF headers, AV1 panic and oversize allocations,
    MPEG-2 allocations, damaged MP4 audio, oversized .3dl LUTs and
    deeply nested CLI parameters; new fuzz tests
  * Timeline and UI: track colour labels, interface animations can
    be turned off, View > Reset Interface Zoom, caption text/timing
    in the Properties panel, Essential Graphics stopwatches, capped
    thumbnail texture cache, complete German translation
  * Export and CLI: SDR exports tagged with a colr box,
    file.exportMedia waits for the export, stricter CLI render and
    number-field parsing, preview files read in place
  * Audio and captions: a failed audio output is re-opened during
    playback, TTML tick rate follows the frame rate, TTS fixes for
    prices, negative amounts and "a.m."
  * Faster AAF export of many markers, AAF/OMF import keeps
    existing files, auto-save rotation keeps the newest file
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list
  * Re-vendored with update=false against the new Cargo.lock
    (respect-lockfile true): vendored crate set unchanged; the only
    new edge in the shipped targets is tempfile 3.27.0 (MIT OR
    Apache-2.0, already vendored), so the licence set and the
    Legal-Review-Notice stay current; no new system deps, MSRV
    still 1.95; cargo_vendor audit clean (no RUSTSEC advisories)
- filmcraft-no-brand-assets.patch still applies unchanged (no fuzz);
  no new docs/brand references in the 0.12.0 tree
- Bump the fixed metainfo release date to 2026-10-23

