Tue Oct 13 07:45:16 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.7.2 (upstream tags v0.6.0, 2026-10-11 and
  v0.7.2, 2026-10-12):
  * New clean-room codecs, all in-tree with no new system
    dependency: VP8/WebM video, MPEG Layer I/II audio, E-AC-3,
    AVI/OpenDML demuxer, FLAC encoder, CinemaDNG/DNG stills,
    AAC audio export, ProRes 4444/XQ with alpha, compressed
    OpenEXR, JPEG/Targa/DPX sequences, GIF/APNG import
  * Hardware: Linux NVDEC (H.264/HEVC) decode and NVENC (H.265)
    export, shared VA-API display, AV1 hardware export
  * Harden the AAF/CFB parsers against malicious files (bounded
    weak-reference and DIFAT/FAT walks); no CVE assigned
  * Faster AV1/HEVC/VP9 decode, exact Matroska/MP3 audio trims,
    Scene Edit Detection, Optical Flow interpolation, Morph Cut,
    8-channel AAC, new interface translations (Japanese, German,
    French, Russian, Ukrainian, Chinese, Indonesian, Portuguese)
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list
- Re-vendored with update=false against the new Cargo.lock (no
  vendor/ shipped upstream; audit findings all outside the
  shipped binaries)
- filmcraft-no-brand-assets.patch still applies unchanged

