Sun Oct 11 06:59:28 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package filmcraft 0.5.0 (upstream tag v0.5.0, 2026-10-10):
  from-scratch Rust workspace source build (resolver 3, edition
  2024, MSRV 1.95); no distro packages it and the home: copy is a
  binary repack, so port the Publishing photocraft structure instead
- Services: tar_scm pinned tag + cargo_vendor (update=false,
  respect-lockfile) + cargo_audit; tarball excludes docs/brand/
  trademarks; build filmcraft + filmcraft-cli --locked --offline
  with default features (whisper off, CRAFT_FONTS_DIR unset)
- License covers the linked MPL-2.0 symphonia decoders (interim
  MP3/FLAC/ALAC/Vorbis) plus embedded OFL-1.1/Ubuntu-font-1.0/
  ISC/Unicode-3.0/Zlib, see the Legal-Review-Notice in the spec
- Add filmcraft-no-brand-assets.patch: point the trademarked
  include_bytes! in crates/ui-egui/src/brand.rs at the open-source
  FilmCraft tile (docs/brand/ stays excluded from tarball and RPM)
- Split out filmcraft-cli subpackage (mirror Publishing/pdfcraft):
  headless exporter/command runner moves to its own package, desktop
  keeps the GUI; main Recommends: filmcraft-cli

